    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_772128eaa802775611c1981d84dc1b3e315e951cddc8c0e79185e05eb8b77dce",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A real sheet that does not meet the critical line carries its unique zeta zero on the left; from such a zero, increasing-modulus constant-argument paths cannot cross or touch the critical line, so their returning families force a separating derivative critical point on the left. Conversely, a left derivative zero supplies decreasing- and increasing-modulus routes whose critical-line enclosure forces a left zeta zero, linking the sheet and derivative criteria through the same routing obstruction.",
